{
  "about": "What each query in the vocabulary can answer, read by the relevance gate (bin/lib/genui_tiers.py `relevance`, docs/reference/GENUI.md 'Relevance gate'). `entities` are the things a query holds, `measures` what it can say about them. Written from each query's own description (bin/kyber-genui builtin_queries and config/surfaces/genui-queries.json) plus the plain synonyms a person says for the same thing, never from a bench request. A word here is evidence a request is about this query; a request whose subject names a word only another query covers is refused for this one. `ask` is what the pill says when the subject is this query's but its required argument is missing. A provider may also declare `covers` in its own manifest entry; that wins over this file.",
